# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

**/*.lock
# …except the Cargo lockfile: binaries commit it (Cargo's guidance), so a dependency regression
# can only arrive as a reviewable `cargo update` commit — never ambush a CI run — and the RustSec
# audit scans the exact resolution every build uses.
!Cargo.lock
config/settings.yaml
.fmp_cache/
.folioman_turnover_*.txt
.folioman_net_stamp
.sec_cache

# screen run-to-run gate state (EXIT-review footer)
.screen_state.json

# the Pages payload (screen's three #1 rows). Written every run; the site's copy is built on the
# runner and uploaded as an artifact, so a committed one would only ever be someone's stale local run.
.screen_web.json

# alert run-to-run market entry state (flip-ping dedup)
.alert_state

# alert per-ticker dip dedup (tickers already pinged; recovery clears)
.alert_dips

# (#333) `.screen_snapshots.jsonl` IS TRACKED — it used to be listed here, and that was the defect.
# It is the ranked-snapshot journal, one line per screen day, and the record all five of `track`'s
# forward sections read. Every one of them needs 12 MONTHLY lines before its verdict can say anything
# but "wait", so the file has to survive a year of probe runs to be worth anything. Untracked it did
# not: 48 lines spanning 2026-07-16..09-08 were lost to a probe's backup/restore, silently, leaving
# one line behind. `append_snapshot` is append-only and never truncates, so the code was never the
# culprit — the missing history was. Tracked, a stray write is a visible diff and one `git checkout`
# undoes it. ~843 B a line, and the Pages job commits each day's line back.
#
# The `.screen_web.json` reasoning four entries up does NOT carry over. That file is a SNAPSHOT, so a
# committed copy is only ever someone's stale local run; this one is append-only HISTORY, where a
# local run's line is a contribution rather than a staleness.

# wide-backtest method verdict (written by `backtest universe`; the screen footer cites it)
.backtest_verdict.json
# its point-in-time twin (written by `backtest universe … pit`; screen's BUY NOW record line cites it)
.backtest_sized.json

# Trading212 tradable-instrument list (weekly cache; order-glue symbol resolution)
.t212_instruments.json

# persistent ISIN -> Yahoo-symbol resolutions (positive-only; stabilizes the ETF universe)
.isin_cache.json
# US symbol -> Xetra twin (OpenFIGI); empty value = resolved to "no usable twin", never re-asked
.eu_listing_cache.json
# last-good venue ISIN lists (fallback across venue outages)
.venue_isins.json
# weekly ESMA+FCA FIRDS ETF-ISIN scan (regulatory universe source)
.regulatory_isins.json
# definitive Yahoo "no such ISIN" answers for regulatory-sourced ISINs (30-day TTL)
.isin_negative_cache.json
# weekly Yahoo quoteSummary TER/AUM for funds missing BF facts
.fund_facts_cache.json
# tickers whose MAX-monthly history added no bars beyond the daily window (30-day TTL)
.long_history_skip.json
.long_history_cache.json
# ...except the frozen 200-ticker copy. No leading slash above, so that pattern matches at ANY depth
# and would swallow the fixture too — and an ignored fixture is an unrunnable pin: tests/backtest_fixture.rs
# is the only end-to-end net over real data, and it must work on a fresh clone and in CI.
!tests/fixture/.long_history_cache.json
.holdings_cache.json
# (PIT) point-in-time S&P 500 membership spans. No TTL by design — `rm` it to refresh; the reasoning
# is on `fetch::SP500_HISTORY_CACHE_PATH`.
.sp500_history.json
# ...except the fixture copy, for the same reason the frozen history cache above is kept: without it
# `backtest … pit` has no offline pin at all, and the one mode nothing can reach is the one that rots.
!tests/fixture/.sp500_history.json
.screen_alerts.log
